      "value": "@{5a4aaf7f758fa46d131cd36b|full_name}: I admit in very few cases, such as with shaders, an avatar might look worse off performance wise than it actually is, but the majority of cases of avatars being bad is with them having a ridiculous amount of materials/skinned mesh renderers or having 50 long chain of dynamic bones with colliders on each and every one on their fingers. Being able to confirm that would be very valuable to me and several others.\n\nThe positives severely outweights the potential negatives to me,  making this suggestion a good first step at least.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
